# LED Matrix Display Example

Renders text on a simulated LED matrix display using the `LEDMatrixDisplayNode`.

## Nodes Used

- `utility/value/constant` — provides the text to display
- `output/display/ledMatrix` — renders text as an LED matrix visualization

The `LEDMatrixDisplayNode` offers configurable:
- Matrix width and height
- LED pixel size and spacing
- Foreground and background colors

## Graph

1. Add a `Constant` node (Utility → Value), set its value to text (e.g., "HELLO LED")
2. Add an `LEDMatrixDisplay` node (Output → LED Matrix)
3. Connect `Constant.output` → `LEDMatrixDisplay.value`

## Pre-made Graph

Import `led-matrix.json` to load the wired graph instantly.

## Build & Run

```bash
cmake --build --preset debug
./build/debug/examples/led-matrix/LedMatrixApp
```
